  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Stroke to Fill Text\n\nDraws type as an outline, then floods each letter solid with a soft edge, in the direction you choose.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A bold word should first read as a blueprint outline, then solidify: an editorial, confident reveal.\n- Large display type where the stroke shows clearly.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text is small: the outline will not read, use split-text-chars.\n- You want a hand-drawn stroke: use handwriting-text.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Fill it in.\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 120\n- color (color): Color, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Font weight, default 800\n- font (enum): Font, default \"poppins\"\n- mode (enum): Split by, default \"chars\"\n- order (enum): Order, default \"start\"\n- stagger_frames (number, 0-20): Stagger, default 3\n- duration_frames (number, 1-90): Unit duration, default 24\n- delay_frames (number, 0-120): Delay, default 6\n- exit (boolean): Exit, default false\n- stroke_color (color): Stroke color, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- stroke_width (number, 0.5-16): Stroke width, default 3\n- direction (enum): Fill direction, default \"up\"\n- edge_softness (number, 0-1): Edge softness, default 0.12\n- stroke_retain (number, 0-1): Stroke kept, default 0.35\n- outline_frames (number, 1-90): Outline fade-in, default 16\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
